Z||000000||saleenfiero||01-23-2001||01:37 PM||||HELP.  Fiero's parked outside, I go out play around with the stereo (as in take it out, plug in the pre-outs and put it bank in.  Now I crank the car over and it won't start!  I mean no cranking at all.  Just put in a new battery, all accessories work fine fuse panel looks good.  What am I missing guys?  Fuel pump works too if that matters.<P>------------------<BR>'86 SE - My car is actually a MacLaren F1 with a Fiero body kit; or not.||||reg||9
Z||000001||Tigger||01-23-2001||01:49 PM||||My first guess would be to try banging on the starter.  Tap it lightly a couple times with a hammer or wrench.  Then see if it starts.  If it starts, I'd replace the solenoid/starter or both as they are probably starting to go bad. <p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 01-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||01-23-2001||03:06 PM||||Automatic or manual transmission?<BR>Automatic: sure it's in park?<BR>Stick: got the clutch pedal depressed all the way?<BR>Other: might have a bad fuse link.||||reg||1
Z||000003||TheHans||01-23-2001||03:22 PM||||I would suggest starting with the starter/sol.<BR>If it is an Auto you might also try the p/n safety switch.<BR>Same thing just happened to my friends pickup we put a paper clip in the switch and it worked. Henceforth proceeded to replace the switch. <BR>Keep posted.||||reg||1
